From 2c97351ba05c794e99fa9de5da5ad2e53ad9d51d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:32:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(adaptive): re-measure the STEP bore's heavy Adaptive pin
 after #839

PR #839 (merge 575f02d8) caps the STEP chord at 0.005 mm, so the user's
bore in Milling-test.step is meshed far finer; on the new outline the
Z 10 level's HSM plan crosses itself and Offset rings cut it, as Z 20
already did. Measured: 575f02d8^1 passes (Z 20 only, 5530/5497/600);
575f02d8 and main f490458a give Z 20 + Z 10, 6500/6464/222, warnings
empty. The pin now asserts exactly {Z 20, Z 10}, each "crosses itself",
and 6500/6464/222; every safety assertion is unchanged. Three release
runs identical. Getting the Z 10 plan back is #980 part 2.

Refs #980

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs | 29 +++++++++++++++++-------
 docs/decisions/980-bore-pin.md   | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 docs/decisions/980-bore-pin.md

diff --git a/crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs b/crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs
